import Frame from "./Frame.astro";
---

<Frame caption="Terminal · infra" fig="Fig. 04" note="The agent searched first, and skipped an afternoon of debugging">
  <div class="rounded-md border border-bp-rule/80 bg-[#06142a] p-4 font-plex-mono text-[12.5px] leading-[1.7] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
    <p>
      <span class="text-bp-gold">you ›</span>{" "}
      <span class="text-bp-ink">the deploy fails with "Not authorized to perform sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity". seen this before?</span>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-bp-faint">
      <span class="text-bp-teal">●</span> chronicle · search_knowledge("AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity")
    </p>
    <p class="pl-4 text-bp-faint">└ 1 gotcha · infra · established ×2</p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      <span class="text-bp-blue">agent ›</span>{" "}
      <span class="text-bp-dim"
        >Yes, in infra last week. For jobs with <span class="text-bp-ink">environment:</span>, the OIDC token's sub is{" "}
        <span class="text-bp-ink">repo:ORG/REPO:environment:NAME</span>, so a trust policy matching the branch fails. I'll match
        the environment instead.</span
      >
    </p>
  </div>
</Frame>
